# Document new test/run commands in README

Whenever you add, rename, or change how to invoke a **runnable entry point** for local testing — including:

- `python -m ...` module CLIs
- scripts under `modes/`
- new argparse subcommands on an existing module
- pytest targets that are meant to be run manually as a smoke/check

you **must** update [README.md](README.md) in the same change.

## What to add

Under the appropriate "Commands by module" (or "Upcoming") section, document:

1. The exact command(s) to run (prefer `.venv` / `python -m ...` forms used in this repo)
2. A short plain-English description of what it does
3. At least one concrete example with realistic arguments (URL, query string, flags)

## Do not

- Leave new CLIs only discoverable via `--help`
- Document secrets or real API keys — point at `.env.example` instead
- Remove existing command docs unless the entry point was deleted (then remove or mark removed)

## Checklist before finishing the task

- [ ] README lists every new/changed command with an example
- [ ] Examples match the actual argparse/API surface you shipped
